Not necessarily. While emphasizing individual responsibility can sometimes deflect attention from systemic issues, it doesn't inherently undermine collective justice. A balanced approach acknowledges both individual accountability and the societal factors that shape behavior, recognizing that true justice requires addressing both personal actions and the structures that enable inequity.<end_of_turn>

